.git
.venv
venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
instance/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep
data/*.csv
data/*.pcap
data/raw/

# Runtime image does not need test, training, or evidence files. Excluding
# them also stops Trivy from scanning our own SBOM/audit JSON as if it were
# installed software (which produced false-positive package findings).
#
# Exception: app.py imports training.model_registry (stdlib-only) for the
# signed registry and deployment check, and joblib unpickles the served
# pipeline, whose classes live in training.preprocessor. Excluding the whole
# package made the container unable to boot, so keep exactly the modules the
# serving path needs.
training/**
!training/__init__.py
!training/model_registry.py
!training/preprocessor.py
docs/*
!docs/summary_metrics.json
tests/
scripts/
models/eval_cache/
docs/figures/
*.md
!models/README.md

